0. COMMON WALL PLATFORM

Before specifying the five wall types, establish the common interface.

The five walls are not five unrelated products.

They are modules occupying the same structural/service envelope.

0.1 Standard Wall Bay

Baseline development geometry:

- Nominal structural bay: compatible with 2×4-class framing.
- Development panel width: target 24 in or 48 in modular increments.
- Panel height: target 8 ft, with alternate 4 ft modules.
- Panel thickness: TBD by structural/acoustic/thermal requirements.
- Structural framing: SUNFORGE or AMBIENTFORGE member family.
- Panel attachment: captive mechanical locking system.
- No permanent adhesive required for primary installation.
- Individual panel removable without destroying adjacent panels.
- Utility cavity maintained behind functional panel.
- Standardized mechanical attachment points.
- Standardized electrical/data pathway.
- Optional fluid pathway where application requires it.
- Replaceable surface layer wherever economically justified.

0.2 Common Interface Components

Structural Receiver Rail

Candidate:

- formed aluminum
- structural steel
- engineered corrosion-resistant metal alloy

Function:

- transfers panel loads into structural frame
- establishes panel alignment
- provides repeatable installation geometry

Mechanical Lock

Candidate mechanisms:

- quarter-turn captive fastener
- wedge lock
- cam lock
- dovetail capture
- spring-loaded locking pin

Requirements:

- positive mechanical retention
- visible locked/unlocked indication
- tool-accessible emergency release
- no permanent adhesive dependency

Service Chase

Provide standardized vertical/horizontal pathways for:

- electrical
- data
- sensor wiring
- low-voltage controls
- optional water
- optional condensate
- optional ventilation

Critical rule:

SERVICES·ARE·ACCESSIBLE·WITHOUT·DESTROYING·THE·WALL.

Panel Gasket

Candidate:

- EPDM
- silicone
- other application-specific elastomer

Functions:

- vibration isolation
- air sealing
- water management where required
- tolerance compensation

Fasteners

Default development candidate:

- stainless steel
- corrosion-resistant structural fasteners

Final grade determined by environment.

Surface Interface

Common mechanical attachment permitting:

- decorative skin
- acoustic skin
- waterproof skin
- translucent skin
- plant cartridge
- maintenance access panel

