6. THE COMMON DESIGN RULE

These five walls should share 80% of their mechanical DNA while differing radically in what they do.

That means a manufacturer doesn't need five factories.

They need:

ONE·FRAME·SYSTEM

ONE·LOCKING·SYSTEM

ONE·SERVICE·SYSTEM

ONE·PANEL·DIMENSION·SYSTEM

ONE·REPAIR·PHILOSOPHY

Then the functional layer changes.

That is where the economics become interesting.

A contractor learns one installation system.

A builder stocks one family of connectors.

A homeowner learns one repair method.

Architects get a library of functions rather than a catalog of unrelated products.

And drywall's replacement isn't:

«"Here is another sheet material."»

It's:

«"Why are we still building every wall as if its only job is to separate two rooms?"»

That is the actual invention target.

