6. DEWALL

BEKW-CODE | Atmospheric Water / Dehumidifying Wall

Purpose: Turn a wall into a controlled moisture-management appliance rather than allowing humidity to become mold's roommate.

The fundamental idea is beautifully simple:

> Give humid air somewhere useful to go.



CORE CONSTRUCTION

The DEWALL is a multilayer wall cassette:

ROOM AIR → PRE-FILTER → AIR CHANNEL → CONDENSATION SURFACE → DRAINAGE PLANE → SERVICE CHASE → STRUCTURAL BACK

The room-facing surface isn't drywall. It's a washable, nonporous architectural panel.

Behind it is a deliberately engineered air path.

CONDENSATION CORE

A thermally conductive fin matrix provides enormous surface area.

Possible construction:

anodized aluminum fin cassette

thermally conductive polymer components where electrical isolation is desirable

hydrophilic condensate surface treatment

continuous gravity drainage channel

removable condensate tray


The objective isn't merely "make something cold."

It's:

AIRFLOW × SURFACE AREA × TEMPERATURE DIFFERENTIAL × RESIDENCE TIME

That becomes the wall's moisture-processing equation.

WATER PATH

Condensate never enters the structural material.

It falls onto:

FIN → COLLECTION CHANNEL → VERTICAL DRAIN → SEALED RESERVOIR / DRAIN

No mystery cavity.

No wet insulation.

No hidden sponge.

No "we'll just hope it dries."

SERVICEABILITY

The room-facing architectural skin releases from the structural cassette.

Behind it:

fan

condensate sensor

drain

filter

electrical bus

optional thermoelectric module

optional heat-exchanger interface


All accessible.

PIEZO OPPORTUNITY

Every airflow-producing component creates vibration.

So the DEWALL can contain a small piezoelectric harvest layer around mechanically active fan mounts.

Not pretending we're powering the house with it.

Just:

movement that already exists → tiny electrical contribution.

THE REALLY FUN PART

Multiple DEWALL cassettes can communicate.

One wall detects:

RH ↑

Another detects:

CONDENSATION LOAD ↑

The system can preferentially route airflow toward the highest-moisture zone.

The wall becomes a distributed environmental organ.


